    "body": "This issue appears to be a duplicate of:\n\n- #54085\n\n**If this is indeed a duplicate:**\nPlease close this issue and subscribe to the linked issue for updates (select \"Close as not planned\" → \"Duplicate\")\n\n**If this is a different issue:**\nNo action needed. A maintainer will review this shortly.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Why were these issues selected?</summary>\n\n**#54085:** Both issues show the exact same error pattern: 'invalid tag' with mangled container names. Issue #54452 shows 'abcde_-5780961788c2d36-features' (space at position 6 becomes '_-'), and #54085 shows 'go___e-ddcb0d3229c9f2c2-features' (spaces/special chars become '___e-'). Both involve features and intermediate builds, suggesting the same tag generation logic is failing.\n\n**Shared root cause:** Docker tag generation bug when container names contain spaces - the space character is being converted to an underscore followed by additional characters, creating invalid Docker tag names\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<sub>This is an automated analysis and might be incorrect.</sub>",
